



# TASK: Vietnamese Mechanical Careers — Cinematic 3D Web Presentation

## OBJECTIVE

Build a **cinematic, 3D-driven, playful-yet-premium web presentation** about:

**GIỚI THIỆU CÁC NGHỀ TRONG LĨNH VỰC CƠ KHÍ**

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Audience | Vietnamese middle-school students, ages 12–15 |
| Language | 100 % Vietnamese — headings, body, labels, tooltips, buttons, error states |
| Slide count | 23 slides |
| Format | Single-page web app, vanilla HTML + CSS + JS + Three.js via CDN |
| Aspect ratio | 16 : 9 (1920 × 1080 reference) |
| Deployment | Static files — works from `file://`, any web server, GitHub Pages, Vercel, Netlify |
| Offline | Must work offline after first load — all assets embedded or cached |

This should feel like **if Duolingo's design team collaborated with Apple's product-page engineers to teach Vietnamese 13-year-olds about mechanical careers.** Warm, playful, premium, surprisingly delightful — never childish, never corporate.

