# 1. DESIGN SOUL

### 1A. The Feeling

| Word | What it means here |
|---|---|
| **Playful** | Objects bounce softly on entrance. Gears wobble when hovered. Numbers count up with spring overshoot. Tooltips appear with a little pop. Nothing is stiff or rigid. |
| **Light** | The page breathes. Backgrounds are creamy and airy. Shadows are soft and wide. Nothing feels heavy or dense. |
| **Warm** | Every color leans toward yellow/orange undertones. Metals are gold-ish. Shadows are warm brown, never blue-gray. Lighting is "golden hour in a clean workshop." |
| **Premium** | Typography is precise. Spacing is generous. Details are polished (rounded corners, consistent radii, considered icon sizes). Nothing looks rushed. |
| **Trustworthy** | Real industrial photographs. Accurate Vietnamese. No exaggerated claims. Real 3D models of real machines. |

### 1B. What This Is NOT

- ❌ Dark-mode tech demo (too intimidating for 13-year-olds)
- ❌ Pastel kawaii cartoon (too young — students are 12–15, not 6)
- ❌ Corporate annual report (boring)
- ❌ AI-generated template (soulless)
- ❌ Bootstrap landing page (generic)
- ❌ Single-color monochrome (lifeless)
- ❌ Neon/cyberpunk (distracting, cold)
- ❌ Full of meaningless 3D decorations (every 3D object must teach something)

### 1C. Layout Philosophy

Every slide follows the **"one idea, one hero, one action"** rule:

- **One idea:** A single concept the student should remember.
- **One hero:** A dominant visual element (3D model, photo, diagram) that occupies 50–70% of the slide.
- **One action:** Something the student can do (hover a part, click to explode, drag to rotate) or passively experience (camera orbit, count-up animation).

**Layout variety is mandatory.** The 23 slides use at least 10 distinct layout archetypes. No two consecutive slides share the same structure.

| Archetype | Used in slides (suggested) |
|---|---|
| Full-bleed 3D + text overlay | 01, 10, 16, 23 |
| Split: 3D left, text right | 03, 07, 14 |
| Split: text left, 3D right | 09, 22 |
| Full-bleed 3D + floating cards | 04, 06 |
| Top strip (photo/3D) + text bottom | 08, 13 |
| Centered 3D + surrounding labels | 05, 12, 15, 21 |
| 2×2 or 2×3 grid | 18, 19, 20 |
| Pull-quote + small visual | 02 |
| Diagonal composition | 11 |
| Minimal: centered text + small accent | 23 |

